WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Your plans change. Your commitments don’t change with them.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Maya’s parents move Friday arrival to Saturday morning; guests go from two to three. The browser lists seven MCP tools.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The baseline still ends Sunday at 17:00, and its existing commitments have not moved.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Seven operations are proposed. Sunday departure stays fixed; existing commitments are unchanged.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:47.000
I review only the arrival-day restaurant cancellation and its simulated $75 fee.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:58.000
I approve that exact operation. Approval changes no commitment; execution is still separate.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:10.000
I execute separately. One cancellation completes, and the other six proposals await decisions.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
The browser briefly shows actual initialize, tools/list, and tools/call request/response evidence.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:36.000
The server ends with six live commitments, six open decisions, and one simulated $75 sunk fee.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:45.850
The $329 of $300 is a projection including pending proposals, not completed spend. Services and fees are fictional.
